{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>From twenty years old and upward.</b> But those younger than twenty are not punished by Heaven and are not required to bring atonement. And the total of all of them amounts to ten thousand talents of silver. How so? Most people live only seventy years; subtract twenty of them for exemption, as it is written, 'from twenty years old and upward,' leaving fifty years. Every single person of Israel gives during them a profane mina per year for the half-shekel, 'a holy shekel,' year after year. Thus sixty men give in their lifetimes sixty minas, which are one talent, and they were sixty myriads; so all of them give ten thousand talents. Therefore the wicked Haman said, 'ten thousand talents of silver I will weigh' — he said: my shekels are worth it to annul their shekels, and I will give against the sixty myriads among them, to do with them as I please."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:01:13.801339019Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}